### ====================================================================
### Bookstore REST API - HTTP Client Collection (Practice 5: AOP & Caching)
### Covers: CRUD endpoints, Read-Heavy Caching (GET /{id} & GET /catalog),
###         Cache Eviction/Refresh on POST/PUT/DELETE, AOP Execution Timing
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/books

### 1. [GET] Read-Heavy Endpoint #1: Get Book by ID (1st call -> Cache MISS, queries DB)
GET {{baseUrl}}/1
Accept: application/json

### 2. [GET] Read-Heavy Endpoint #1: Get Book by ID (2nd call -> Cache HIT, 0ms DB skip!)
GET {{baseUrl}}/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. [GET] Read-Heavy Endpoint #2: Full Book Catalog (1st call -> Cache MISS)
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog
Accept: application/json

### 4. [GET] Read-Heavy Endpoint #2: Full Book Catalog (2nd call -> Cache HIT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog
Accept: application/json

### 5. [POST] Create a new Book (Evicts 'booksList' cache)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "AspectJ in Action",
  "author": "Ramnivas Laddad",
  "isbn": "9781933988054",
  "price": 47.99,
  "publicationYear": 2009,
  "description": "Enterprise AOP with Spring Applications"
}

### 6. [PUT] Update existing Book by ID (Refreshes 'books' cache via @CachePut & evicts 'booksList')
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code (Cached & Updated Edition)",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "isbn": "9780132350884",
  "price": 41.99,
  "publicationYear": 2008,
  "description": "Updated book entry automatically refreshed in Caffeine cache"
}

### 7. [GET] Verify updated book is served immediately from updated cache
GET {{baseUrl}}/1
Accept: application/json

### 8. [DELETE] Delete book by ID (Evicts both 'books' key and 'booksList' cache)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/1

### 9. [GET] Paginated list of books
GET {{baseUrl}}?page=0&size=5&sort=title,asc
Accept: application/json
